  "result": "Perfect! All 249 tests pass. The late fee feature is now fully implemented and tested. Here's what was added:\n\n**Changes Made:**\n\n1. **Added `lateFee(invoice, asOf)` to `src/reports.js`**:\n   - Calculates late fees for overdue invoices\n   - Formula: 0.04% per day of the amount still due\n   - Returns 0 if invoice is not overdue (dueDate >= asOf)\n   - Calculation: `due * 0.0004 * daysOverdue`\n   - Uses `roundCents()` for proper rounding\n   - Uses `balanceDue()` to respect payments\n   - Uses `daysBetween()` for accurate date calculations\n\n2. **Key Features:**\n   - Proper date comparison (non-overdue on due date)\n   - Respects payment history (uses balanceDue)\n   - Accurate daily accrual calculation\n   - Proper rounding using banker's rounding\n   - Works with all invoice types (issued, partially_paid, paid)\n   - Handles edge cases (zero balance, draft invoices, etc.)\n\n3. **Comprehensive test suite** with 16 tests in `test/reports.test.js` covering:\n   - Non-overdue invoices return 0\n   - Due date equals asOf returns 0\n   - Overdue invoices calculate fee\n   - Correct 0.04% per day rate\n   - Paid invoices return 0\n   - Partially paid invoices calculate on remaining balance\n   - Fee growth with days overdue\n   - Zero balance due returns 0\n   - Large invoice amounts\n   - Small invoice amounts\n   - One day overdue calculation\n   - Ten days overdue calculation\n   - EOM terms handling\n   - Discounted invoice handling\n   - Long-term accumulation (61 days)\n\nThe late fee system provides automatic calculation of penalty interest for overdue invoices, using a daily accrual rate of 0.04%, and properly respecting all invoice modifications and payment history.",
